  "notes": [
    "Generation mapping: heating_rate = -ln(1-g)/t_cycle and cz_leak_prob = 8e-4*(g/g_default), with g_default = 1-exp(-Gamma0*t_cycle), Gamma0 = 1/(700 us). At g_default these are the literature-default channels; at g=0 both creation channels are off. The 2023 SI channel ratio is preserved.",
    "Using LeakageParams defaults: t_cycle=8.96e-07 seconds; g_default=0.001279181149413514. Transport and seepage retain engine defaults.",
    "The readout path is readout_leak_prob = multiplier*g per measurement.",
    "Rise and covariance are reported, not gated, because the supplement states no uncertainties for S23/S24 and no detector-level target data is public (SME major 6).",
    "Arm 4 is a prediction, not a fit. removal_boost (default 5.0) is the v0 Miao-efficacy stand-in, not a fitted efficacy.",
    "Results from this code at reduced scale are machinery demonstrations, not a verdict on the paper's attribution.",
    "ratio_tolerance=5.0 is caller-supplied. Joint scoring uses target_ratio=6.6 and population_ceiling=0.01; the default ratio target 6.6 is the rounded LITERATURE comparison 5.3/0.8.",
    "Baseline ratios against themselves are null. Leakage ratio_ci results use error counts and retained shots at each N. The baseline cross-check LER ratio uses per-cycle rates at the largest N.",
    "The cross-check chi-square uses the smaller retained shot count because detection_curve_chi2 accepts one common count; with unequal postselected counts this is a conservative common-count approximation.",
    "Logical failure means any observable prediction differs from its sampled flip. Covariance uses retained detector events. The population tail starts at floor(curve_length/2).",
    "Undefined or nonfinite numerical results are JSON null; scoring is null when its ratio or population is unavailable. Rise is null if rise_summary raises. No pseudocounts are added by this driver."
  ]
